References: <CZLQA_fqIhU.zP34r1pr-9kJ@lavaan.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/lavaan/c/CZLQA_fqIhU/m/-464rWMlKREJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

You haven't set the scale of f in the analysis model. There are two built in options in lavaan: a marker variable method (setting a factor loading to 1) or a fixed factor method (setting the latent variance/residual variance to 1). By default the cfa command will use a marker variable method, but in your code you overwrote that (by using the NA label on the first factor loading). Either add std.lv <http://std.lv>=TRUE to the cfa function in your loop, or remove the NA* from the model syntax and things should run fine.*

Alex

* Fun fact, tests of significance (using a Wald test) will differ depending on how you set the scale, so depending on the method you use the power results you obtain might be different. The way to avoid this is to use a nested model, likelihood ratio test to test the significance of a parameter.

