This looks fine to me.  Thanks for including a visual prinout of your matrix, but again, it is hard for anyone on the forum to find out what is wrong without being able to reproduce the problem.  I pasted your information and read it into R (version 3.2.1), and I only included rownames for the matrix, not column names (as I saw in your output).  I also got an error message when I used the MBESS function, and the reason is that your correlation matrix doesn't pass the test for being symmetric (if you imported the correlations from a file, there might be a typo in your data):

> > isSymmetric(cor.matrix)
> [1] FALSE

But when I used the lavaan (version 0.5-19.863) function cor2cov() it worked fine for me (see output below signature).

I did notice that in your original message, you referred to an object "sd.vector" using the MBESS function, but you referred to an object "vector.sd <http://vector.sd>" using the lavaan function.  This won't work unless vector.sd <http://vector.sd> == sd.vector.

But the reason for your error message is exactly what it says: you included unused arguments.  That doesn't seem to make sense because "R" and "sds" are existing arguments for the lavaan function.  Therefore, I think that when you called "cor2cov", it was using the MBESS function (perhaps because MBESS was loaded into your workspace after lavaan was).  It will probably work if you tell R to use the lavaan version of that function:

lavaan::cor2cov(R = cor.matrix, sds = sd.vector)

This is why a complete R script to reproduce your problem is always more helpful than a verbal description alone.

Terry

