> In lavData(data = data, group = group, group.label = group.label,  :
>   lavaan WARNING: data argument has been coerced to a data.frame

I can't tell where the error message is coming from.  And the warning about coercing the data argument to a data.frame is unexpected, because your dataMI$imputations should be a list of data.frames already.

> ## this code is working well for all imputed datasets (not just for the first one)
> modelMI_imp1<-sem(myModelSEM,data=data.frame(dataMI$imputations[[1]]), ordered=c("bi1", "bi2", "bi3", "bi4","bi5"))
> summary(modelMI_imp1, fit.measures=TRUE, standardized=TRUE)

Well, if all the data sets can be analyzed fine, the problem might be with combining results, but I'm not sure why that would be happening.  I'm curious to see what will happen after you update semTools and make your imputation model consistent with your analysis model.  You already have to use DWLS because of your binary indicators, but if you want to impute the 5-category items as ordered, treat them as ordered in the analysis too, or treat them as continuous in both.

